{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cg6tUT6T5MZi6ok1JKWBe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All checks are complete and the evidence is recorded. Here is my summary before the structured report:\n\n**What I found (physical review of the saved board and native check outputs):**\n\n- **Native DRC errors are real and physical.** Five J1 connector peg holes are modeled as *plated* through-holes whose drill equals the pad size (4.0/4.0 mm and 2.2/2.2 mm) — zero annular ring, flagged by both `padstack` and `annular_width` error checks. Three GND pads (C14.2, C15.2, U7.4) connect to the saved F.Cu ground fill with only one thermal spoke against the board's own two-spoke minimum.\n- **CAN2 termination (explicitly in scope):** both 120 Ω terminators (R36 at the U20 end, R37 at the U21 end) are DNP in the saved design, so the internal bus linking the ECU module (J2.73/74), both wideband transceivers, and the external pins J1.11/15 (a ~107 mm stub) has **no populated termination anywhere**. Function depends on unverified module/harness termination; fitting both while an external terminated bus is attached would load the bus at 40 Ω. Raised as a major concern.\n- **Current-path geometry:** each wideband heater return is a single 0.6 mm, 35 µm track (112 mm and 158 mm; ~92/129 mΩ, IPC-2221 ≈1.7 A at 10 °C rise vs ~2.5 A heater warm-up current → ~26 °C estimated rise). The ETB1 H-bridge supply pad reaches the power plane solely through a 0.8 mm × 4.6 mm neck via J1.73/74; ETB2 through three 0.4 mm vias. Marginal under stall/current-limit, fine at nominal — concerns, not defects (no thermal qualification inferred from width).\n- **Library resolution defect:** the project fp-lib-table registers only 3 libraries while the board uses `Simon:*` footprints; `fome-kicad-libs/Simon.pretty` exists in-repo but is unregistered, and no `hellen-one-common` symbol library exists at all — matching the 22+ native lib-resolution warnings and the J2 footprint/symbol substitution parity warning.\n- The disposable sheet alias is confirmed: `VR Conditioner.kicad_sch` and `VR conditioner.kicad_sch` are byte-identical (sha256 377a2691…), with both files coexisting.\n- The five ERC errors trace to missing PWR_FLAGs on harness-fed rails, an unmarked NC pin, and paralleled power-output pins in the J2 symbol — hygiene, reported at info level.\n\nAll calculations, commands, and assumptions are in `review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3344,"cache_read_input_tokens":316512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3344},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"295a55b9-1e87-4313-bedf-1a2174d67732","uuid":"8e9089c3-2d60-4b02-a89c-71026f3a1a1a","timestamp":"2026-10-17T00:48:17.692Z","request_id":"req_011Cg6tUS1hiJLsyDMZCmLF5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cg6tUT6T5MZi6ok1JKWBe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013xrarCcRiPV9Bs5ems3qSy","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"46e5a5c34e7b9715155c9e90277cd3639b3a19ebb9590053a081bbb6436ba860","run_id":"8534a2a6-e237-4d1c-a002-90ce37ec09e4","packet_sha256":"98d9c1b6fab29738035a23626c8f92708bf9cb153628d6077ab0ca2e6b9f0340","role":"physical","coverage":["Re-extracted all 13 error-severity items from the full native DRC report (work/drc/drc.json) and localized them on the saved board via the pcbnew API (padstacks, annular width, starved thermals).","Inspected J1 mechanical padstacks directly in the saved .kicad_pcb (pad attribute, size, drill).","Verified the disposable sheet alias: byte-identical sha256 for 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' and 'VR conditioner.kicad_sch'.","Mapped the complete CAN2 physical topology (all pads/nodes, termination resistor placement and DNP state, line-loading capacitors, external-pin stub length).","Measured copper geometry of high-current paths: wideband heater returns (/HeaterNeg, /HeaterNeg2), fused 12V distribution (/12V_MR_FUSE zone, via count, ETB supply necks), ETB motor outputs, unfused /12V_MR feed; computed IPC-2221 ampacity estimates and trace resistances with stated assumptions (review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md).","Enumerated all copper zones and confirmed the two unfilled no-net entries are rule areas, not forgotten fills; confirmed GND plane coverage (F.Cu/In2.Gnd.Cu/B.Cu) and 0 unconnected items at saved fill state.","Checked project library resolution: fp-lib-table/sym-lib-table contents versus libraries actually referenced and library files present in the repo; correlated with the native lib_*_issues warnings and the J2 footprint-substitution parity warning.","Reviewed all 5 native ERC errors from work/erc/erc.json and attributed root causes.","Cross-checked netlist connectivity (work/netlist/connectivity.json) against board pad nets for the nets examined."],"limitations":["Zone fills evaluated as saved; the read-only candidate forbids a refill pass, so fill-dependent results (starved thermals, connectivity) reflect the saved state only.","Ampacity figures are IPC-2221 chart-fit estimates at assumed 35 µm copper and still air; no IPC-2152 lookup, FEA, or measured thermal data — they bound marginality but do not qualify or disqualify the design thermally.","Molex 64333-0100 terminal and Keystone 3568 fuse-clip current ratings were not verified against manufacturer data; connector-pin ampacity is not assessed.","TLE9201SG current-limit and LSU heater current figures are from reviewer knowledge, not freshly retrieved datasheets, and are stated as assumptions in the experiments notes.","Internal construction of the Polygonus brain module and wideband modules (including any on-module CAN termination) is outside the donor and could not be verified.","No EMC, automotive transient, ignition-energy, or wideband control-stability analysis (declared out of scope by the packet).","Whether 'Simon' / 'hellen-one-common' libraries resolve via the original author's global library tables cannot be determined from the candidate."],"findings":[{"id":"PHY-01","title":"J1 mechanical peg holes are plated through-holes with zero annular ring (5 native DRC errors)","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, footprint J1 (Simon:Molex_112_643330100), no-net pads at (71.95,35.49), (75.55,39.34), (120.0,28.49), (199.65,39.34), (203.25,35.49) mm","condition":"Five no-net pads of the 112-pin header are saved as PTH pads whose drill equals the pad size (4.0/4.0 mm ×3, 2.2/2.2 mm ×2), giving 0.000 mm annular width against the board's 0.100 mm minimum; native DRC reports 5 'padstack' and 5 'annular_width' errors.","mechanism":"A plated hole with no copper land either gets rejected/queried at fabrication or is plated anyway, reducing the finished hole diameter by roughly the plating thickness and leaving an unanchored barrel; for connector alignment pegs this risks peg interference fit changes and plating tear-out during connector press-in. The holes should be NPTH.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"violations[] type=padstack and type=annular_width, severity=error, items 'PTH pad [<no net>] of J1'"},{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md","locator":"section 1 — pcbnew pad attribute/size/drill extraction"},{"path":"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb","locator":"footprint J1, no-net thru_hole pads with size==drill"}],"reasoning":"Confirmed directly in the saved board via pcbnew (PTH attribute, size==drill). This is a mechanical/manufacturing issue only (no net attached), so severity is minor, but it is a definite native-rule violation in the saved candidate."},{"id":"PHY-02","title":"Saved F.Cu ground fill leaves three pads with starved thermal reliefs (1 spoke vs required 2)","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, GND zone on F.Cu; pads C15.2 (107.85,98.76), U7.4 (101.01,102.68), C14.2 (101.59,104.29) mm (VR module area)","condition":"Native DRC reports 3 error-severity 'starved_thermal' violations: the saved F.Cu GND fill connects these pads with a single thermal spoke where the zone's own constraint requires a minimum of two.","mechanism":"A single-spoke thermal connection halves the intended copper cross-section at the joint: higher joint resistance/inductance on decoupling and comparator ground pins, and a mechanically/thermally weaker solder connection that is more vulnerable to spoke necking during fill changes or fabrication etch variation.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"violations[] type=starved_thermal, severity=error (3 items)"},{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md","locator":"section 1 and section 5 (saved-fill state, 0 unconnected items)"}],"reasoning":"The pads remain electrically connected (DRC shows 0 unconnected items), so the impact is marginal rather than functional; but it violates the board's own fill constraints in the saved state, which the read-only review must take as-is. Minor defect."},{"id":"PHY-03","title":"Internal dual-wideband CAN2 bus has no populated termination: both 120 Ω terminators (R36, R37) are DNP","location":"wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch (both instances /WBO-CAN-TRANS/ and /WBO-CAN-TRANS1/), R36/R37; board nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2-, R36 at (175.0,140.7), R37 at (81.6,140.6) mm","condition":"The CAN2 bus internally links the ECU module (J2.73/74 at x≈144), both TJA1051T-3 wideband transceivers (U21 at x≈78, U20 at x≈178), and external connector pins J1.11/15 via a ~107 mm stub. The only termination resistors on the net — 120 Ω R36 at the U20 end and 120 Ω R37 at the U21 end — are both marked DNP ((dnp yes), in_bom no) in the saved design, so as-built the bus has zero ohmic termination; line loading is 2×47 pF per line (C29/C33, C30/C34) plus two NUP2105L clamps.","mechanism":"An unterminated high-speed CAN bus has no defined recessive differential load: reflections and slow recessive transitions cause bit errors, and the README-advertised internal wideband function (wideband controllers 'connected internally to CAN bus #2') then depends entirely on termination existing inside the plug-in brain module or in the external harness, neither of which is part of this donor. Conversely, if a builder populates both R36 and R37 and also attaches an externally terminated CAN2 harness through J1.11/15, the bus load falls to ~40 Ω, below the transceiver's normal 50–65 Ω operating load.","severity":"major","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543 (R36/R37, Value 120, dnp yes, in_bom no)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"components R36/R37 dnp:true; nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2- node lists"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"footprint R36 dnp:true, pads on /CAN2+ and /CAN2-"},{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md","locator":"section 3 — CAN2 node map, stub length, line loading"},{"path":"inputs/project/README.md","locator":"'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers … connected internally to CAN bus #2'"}],"reasoning":"Placement of the two terminators at the physical bus ends is correct and the DNP pattern may be a deliberate configuration option, so this is not provable as a defect from the donor alone. But the packet scope explicitly claims 'internal dual-wideband CAN termination', and the saved evidence shows no termination is actually populated: correct operation of an advertised core feature rests on an unverified assumption about the module or harness. Major concern requiring documentation or module-side verification."},{"id":"PHY-04","title":"Wideband heater return currents carried on single 0.6 mm tracks up to 158 mm long","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, nets /HeaterNeg (J1.108 → U1.11/12, ≈112 mm, B.Cu) and /HeaterNeg2 (J1.76 → U2.11/12, ≈158 mm, B.Cu)","condition":"Each wideband sensor heater return is a single 0.6 mm wide, 35 µm thick B.Cu track with no parallel copper and no plane relief: measured R ≈ 92 mΩ (/HeaterNeg) and ≈ 129 mΩ (/HeaterNeg2). IPC-2221 external estimate for 0.6 mm/1 oz is ≈1.65 A at 10 °C rise; at the ~2.5 A LSU heater warm-up current the estimated rise is ≈26 °C (≈39 °C at 3 A) with 0.57–0.81 W dissipated along the trace and 0.23–0.32 V dropped in the heater low side.","mechanism":"During every cold start the heater PWM ramp drives ~2–2.5 A through these traces for tens of seconds to minutes; in an engine-bay ambient the added 25–40 °C self-heating pushes local trace temperature well above the surrounding board, stressing laminate and solder joints over life, and the series drop slightly reduces heater voltage authority available to the module's closed-loop heater control.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md","locator":"section 4 'Heater returns' — pcbnew segment listing, resistance and IPC-2221 calculations with assumptions"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets /HeaterNeg (J1.108, U1.11, U1.12) and /HeaterNeg2 (J1.76, U2.11, U2.12)"},{"path":"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb","locator":"0.6 mm B.Cu segments on /HeaterNeg and /HeaterNeg2"}],"reasoning":"Width alone does not establish a failure — heater current is duty-limited and the estimates are chart fits, so this is a concern, not a defect. It is the thinnest sustained-current copper on the board relative to its expected load and merits either a width increase, paralleled layers, or a documented thermal justification."},{"id":"PHY-05","title":"ETB H-bridge supply pads reach the 12V_MR_FUSE plane through narrow necks and only three 0.4 mm vias net-wide","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, net /12V_MR_FUSE: U15 pad 4 (120.54,44.91) via 0.8 mm×4.6 mm F.Cu neck to J1.73/74 barrels; U3 pad 4 (103.68,45.1) via 0.8 mm×1.6 mm neck and the net's only 3 vias (0.4 mm drill) at (109–111.2,52.5) mm","condition":"The fused 12 V rail is distributed on the In.Power.Cu plane, but the entire net has just three 0.4 mm vias. The ETB1 driver (U15, TLE9201SG, 6 A-class with internal current limit above 6 A) is fed exclusively through a 0.8 mm wide, 4.6 mm long 1 oz F.Cu segment into the J1.73/74 pin barrels; the ETB2 driver (U3) is fed through the three-via group (≈2.3 A each at 10 °C rise estimate, ≈7 A combined).","mechanism":"At nominal throttle currents (1–2 A) the 0.8 mm neck sits near 10 °C rise — acceptable. During motor stall or driver current-limit events (>6 A), IPC-2221 extrapolation puts the 0.8 mm segment above 100 °C rise if sustained; repeated limit/thermal-shutdown cycling of the TLE9201 can hold average current high while the trace, unlike the IC, has no protection. The three-via group for ETB2 is adequate only if current shares evenly and events stay brief.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md","locator":"section 4 'ETB H-bridge supply' — full track/via/pad extraction and IPC-2221 calculations"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"U15 pad 4 /12V_MR_FUSE SMD at (120.54,44.91); U3 pad 4 at (103.68,45.1)"},{"path":"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb","locator":"/12V_MR_FUSE F.Cu tracks (120.56,44.94)→(125.12,44.94) w=0.8; vias at (109.02/110.06/111.17, 52.5)"}],"reasoning":"Short necks tolerate brief overloads and throttle stall events are transient, so no defect is provable; but a 6 A-class bridge fed through a single 0.8 mm neck and a net served by three small vias is marginal by estimate and worth widening or paralleling. Reported as a calculated concern, not a thermal disqualification."},{"id":"PHY-06","title":"Project library tables do not resolve the libraries the design actually uses (Simon footprints unregistered, hellen-one-common absent)","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base project: fp-lib-table (3 entries), sym-lib-table (2 entries) vs references Simon:Molex_112_643330100, Simon:PAD-TH, Simon:BMM-USB, Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD (J2), hellen-one-common symbols (R1–R4, C1, J4, P1–P6)","condition":"fp-lib-table registers only wideband_module, header_placement and fome_modules even though fome-kicad-libs/Simon.pretty exists in the repo; no hellen-one-common library file exists anywhere in the project. Native checks correspondingly report 8 footprint_link_issues and 14 lib_symbol_issues (ERC) plus 9 lib_footprint_issues (DRC), and schematic parity flags that board J2 uses Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD while the symbol specifies fome_modules:polygonus.","mechanism":"The design builds only from the caches embedded in the schematic and board files; a clean checkout cannot re-resolve, diff, or update these footprints/symbols against sources, so library drift (such as the already-present J2 footprint substitution) cannot be audited, and any footprint refresh in KiCad would fail or silently diverge.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/fp-lib-table","locator":"full file — 3 libraries, no 'Simon' entry despite fome-kicad-libs/Simon.pretty in repo"},{"path":"inputs/project/sym-lib-table","locator":"full file — no 'hellen-one-common' entry; no such file found in project tree"},{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"lib_symbol_issues / footprint_link_issues entries citing 'Simon' and 'hellen-one-common'"},{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"schematic_parity: 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)' (J2); lib_footprint_issues for library 'Simon'"}],"reasoning":"The native violations are reproduced from the project's own saved tables, and the unregistered in-repo Simon.pretty shows this is a project-configuration gap rather than purely a sandbox artifact (the possibility of an author-side global table is noted as a limitation). No electrical impact in the saved state since caches are intact — minor defect in manufacturing-data/reproducibility hygiene."},{"id":"PHY-07","title":"Five native ERC errors remain: undriven power-input pins, unmarked NC pin, and paralleled power-output pins","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch root sheet: #PWR01 GND pin (36.8,78.7); A1 pin 8 VMOT (48.3,219.7); J2 pin 90 12V_IGN (293.4,174.0); A1 pin 2 ~FLT (38.1,224.8); J2 pins 40/41 5V_SENSOR_1 (262.9,128.3/130.8)","condition":"ERC reports 5 errors: three power_pin_not_driven (a GND power symbol pin, A1 VMOT on /12V_MR_FUSE, J2.90 12V_IGN on /12V_KEY), one pin_not_connected (A1 ~FLT output with no no-connect marker), and one pin_to_pin (J2 pins 40 and 41 both typed Power output and tied together on 5V_SENSOR_1).","mechanism":"These rails are genuinely fed from the vehicle harness through J1 (12V_KEY: J1.45↔J2.90; 12V_MR_FUSE carries F1 output), so the undriven-pin errors reflect missing PWR_FLAG markers rather than missing supplies; the pin_to_pin error reflects the J2 module symbol modelling its paralleled 5V output pins both as Power output; A1 ~FLT is an open fault output (netlist: unconnected-(A1-~FLT-Pad2)) lacking an NC flag. None indicates a physical copper fault, but unresolved errors mask any future real ERC regressions.","severity":"info","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"severity=error entries: power_pin_not_driven ×3, pin_not_connected (A1 ~FLT), pin_to_pin (J2 40/41)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets /12V_KEY (J1.45,J2.90), /5V_SENSOR_1 (J2.40,J2.41), unconnected-(A1-~FLT-Pad2)"}],"reasoning":"Evidence-supported native errors in the saved schematic; root-cause analysis shows schematic-modelling hygiene (missing PWR_FLAG/NC markers, symbol pin typing) rather than electrical faults, hence info severity. Left at defect because the native rule set is violated as saved and the errors should be resolved or waived explicitly."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3344,"cache_read_input_tokens":316512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3344},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"295a55b9-1e87-4313-bedf-1a2174d67732","uuid":"f3a8381e-291c-41d2-8d04-5e7b9edb1d2e","timestamp":"2026-10-17T00:49:48.696Z","request_id":"req_011Cg6tUS1hiJLsyDMZCmLF5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013xrarCcRiPV9Bs5ems3qSy":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"46e5a5c34e7b9715155c9e90277cd3639b3a19ebb9590053a081bbb6436ba860","run_id":"8534a2a6-e237-4d1c-a002-90ce37ec09e4","packet_sha256":"98d9c1b6fab29738035a23626c8f92708bf9cb153628d6077ab0ca2e6b9f0340","role":"physical","coverage":["Re-extracted all 13 error-severity items from the full native DRC report (work/drc/drc.json) and localized them on the saved board via the pcbnew API (padstacks, annular width, starved thermals).","Inspected J1 mechanical padstacks directly in the saved .kicad_pcb (pad attribute, size, drill).","Verified the disposable sheet alias: byte-identical sha256 for 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' and 'VR conditioner.kicad_sch'.","Mapped the complete CAN2 physical topology (all pads/nodes, termination resistor placement and DNP state, line-loading capacitors, external-pin stub length).","Measured copper geometry of high-current paths: wideband heater returns (/HeaterNeg, /HeaterNeg2), fused 12V distribution (/12V_MR_FUSE zone, via count, ETB supply necks), ETB motor outputs, unfused /12V_MR feed; computed IPC-2221 ampacity estimates and trace resistances with stated assumptions (review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md).","Enumerated all copper zones and confirmed the two unfilled no-net entries are rule areas, not forgotten fills; confirmed GND plane coverage (F.Cu/In2.Gnd.Cu/B.Cu) and 0 unconnected items at saved fill state.","Checked project library resolution: fp-lib-table/sym-lib-table contents versus libraries actually referenced and library files present in the repo; correlated with the native lib_*_issues warnings and the J2 footprint-substitution parity warning.","Reviewed all 5 native ERC errors from work/erc/erc.json and attributed root causes.","Cross-checked netlist connectivity (work/netlist/connectivity.json) against board pad nets for the nets examined."],"limitations":["Zone fills evaluated as saved; the read-only candidate forbids a refill pass, so fill-dependent results (starved thermals, connectivity) reflect the saved state only.","Ampacity figures are IPC-2221 chart-f