ocator":"'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers … connected internally to CAN bus #2'"}],"reasoning":"Placement of the two terminators at the physical bus ends is correct and the DNP pattern may be a deliberate configuration option, so this is not provable as a defect from the donor alone. But the packet scope explicitly claims 'internal dual-wideband CAN termination', and the saved evidence shows no termination is actually populated: correct operation of an advertised core feature rests on an unverified assumption about the module or harness. Major concern requiring documentation or module-side verification."},{"id":"PHY-04","title":"Wideband heater return currents carried on single 0.6 mm tracks up to 158 mm long","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, nets /HeaterNeg (J1.108 → U1.11/12, ≈112 mm, B.Cu) and /HeaterNeg2 (J1.76 → U2.11/12, ≈158 mm, B.Cu)","condition":"Each wideband sensor heater return is a single 0.6 mm wide, 35 µm thick B.Cu track with no parallel copper and no plane relief: measured R ≈ 92 mΩ (/HeaterNeg) and ≈ 129 mΩ (/HeaterNeg2). IPC-2221 external estimate for 0.6 mm/1 oz is ≈1.65 A at 10 °C rise; at the ~2.5 A LSU heater warm-up current the estimated rise is ≈26 °C (≈39 °C at 3 A) with 0.57–0.81 W dissipated along the trace and 0.23–0.32 V dropped in the heater low side.","mechanism":"During every cold start the heater PWM ramp drives ~2–2.5 A through these traces for tens of seconds to minutes; in an engine-bay ambient the added 25–40 °C self-heating pushes local trace temperature well above the surrounding board, stressing laminate and solder joints over life, and the series drop slightly reduces heater voltage authority available to the module's closed-loop heater control.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md","locator":"section 4 'Heater returns' — pcbnew segment listing, resistance and IPC-2221 calculations with assumptions"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets /HeaterNeg (J1.108, U1.11, U1.12) and /HeaterNeg2 (J1.76, U2.11, U2.12)"},{"path":"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb","locator":"0.6 mm B.Cu segments on /HeaterNeg and /HeaterNeg2"}],"reasoning":"Width alone does not establish a failure — heater current is duty-limited and the estimates are chart fits, so this is a concern, not a defect. It is the thinnest sustained-current copper on the board relative to its expected load and merits either a width increase, paralleled layers, or a documented thermal justification."},{"id":"PHY-05","title":"ETB H-bridge supply pads reach the 12V_MR_FUSE plane through narrow necks and only three 0.4 mm vias net-wide","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, net /12V_MR_FUSE: U15 pad 4 (120.54,44.91) via 0.8 mm×4.6 mm F.Cu neck to J1.73/74 barrels; U3 pad 4 (103.68,45.1) via 0.8 mm×1.6 mm neck and the net's only 3 vias (0.4 mm drill) at (109–111.2,52.5) mm","condition":"The fused 12 V rail is distributed on the In.Power.Cu plane, but the entire net has just three 0.4 mm vias. The ETB1 driver (U15, TLE9201SG, 6 A-class with internal current limit above 6 A) is fed exclusively through a 0.8 mm wide, 4.6 mm long 1 oz F.Cu segment into the J1.73/74 pin barrels; the ETB2 driver (U3) is fed through the three-via group (≈2.3 A each at 10 °C rise estimate, ≈7 A combined).","mechanism":"At nominal throttle currents (1–2 A) the 0.8 mm neck sits near 10 °C rise — acceptable. During motor stall or driver current-limit events (>6 A), IPC-2221 extrapolation puts the 0.8 mm segment above 100 °C rise if sustained; repeated limit/thermal-shutdown cycling of the TLE9201 can hold average current high while the trace, unlike the IC, has no protection. The three-via group for ETB2 is adequate only if current shares evenly and events stay brief.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md","locator":"section 4 'ETB H-bridge supply' — full track/via/pad extraction and IPC-2221 calculations"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"U15 pad 4 /12V_MR_FUSE SMD at (120.54,44.91); U3 pad 4 at (103.68,45.1)"},{"path":"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb","locator":"/12V_MR_FUSE F.Cu tracks (120.56,44.94)→(125.12,44.94) w=0.8; vias at (109.02/110.06/111.17, 52.5)"}],"reasoning":"Short necks tolerate brief overloads and throttle stall events are transient, so no defect is provable; but a 6 A-class bridge fed through a single 0.8 mm neck and a net served by three small vias is marginal by estimate and worth widening or paralleling. Reported as a calculated concern, not a thermal disqualification."},{"id":"PHY-06","title":"Project library tables do not resolve the libraries the design actually uses (Simon footprints unregistered, hellen-one-common absent)","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base project: fp-lib-table (3 entries), sym-lib-table (2 entries) vs references Simon:Molex_112_643330100, Simon:PAD-TH, Simon:BMM-USB, Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD (J2), hellen-one-common symbols (R1–R4, C1, J4, P1–P6)","condition":"fp-lib-table registers only wideband_module, header_placement and fome_modules even though fome-kicad-libs/Simon.pretty exists in the repo; no hellen-one-common library file exists anywhere in the project. Native checks correspondingly report 8 footprint_link_issues and 14 lib_symbol_issues (ERC) plus 9 lib_footprint_issues (DRC), and schematic parity flags that board J2 uses Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD while the symbol specifies fome_modules:polygonus.","mechanism":"The design builds only from the caches embedded in the schematic and board files; a clean checkout cannot re-resolve, diff, or update these footprints/symbols against sources, so library drift (such as the already-present J2 footprint substitution) cannot be audited, and any footprint refresh in KiCad would fail or silently diverge.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/fp-lib-table","locator":"full file — 3 libraries, no 'Simon' entry despite fome-kicad-libs/Simon.pretty in repo"},{"path":"inputs/project/sym-lib-table","locator":"full file — no 'hellen-one-common' entry; no such file found in project tree"},{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"lib_symbol_issues / footprint_link_issues entries citing 'Simon' and 'hellen-one-common'"},{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"schematic_parity: 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)' (J2); lib_footprint_issues for library 'Simon'"}],"reasoning":"The native violations are reproduced from the project's own saved tables, and the unregistered in-repo Simon.pretty shows this is a project-configuration gap rather than purely a sandbox artifact (the possibility of an author-side global table is noted as a limitation). No electrical impact in the saved state since caches are intact — minor defect in manufacturing-data/reproducibility hygiene."},{"id":"PHY-07","title":"Five native ERC errors remain: undriven power-input pins, unmarked NC pin, and paralleled power-output pins","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch root sheet: #PWR01 GND pin (36.8,78.7); A1 pin 8 VMOT (48.3,219.7); J2 pin 90 12V_IGN (293.4,174.0); A1 pin 2 ~FLT (38.1,224.8); J2 pins 40/41 5V_SENSOR_1 (262.9,128.3/130.8)","condition":"ERC reports 5 errors: three power_pin_not_driven (a GND power symbol pin, A1 VMOT on /12V_MR_FUSE, J2.90 12V_IGN on /12V_KEY), one pin_not_connected (A1 ~FLT output with no no-connect marker), and one pin_to_pin (J2 pins 40 and 41 both typed Power output and tied together on 5V_SENSOR_1).","mechanism":"These rails are genuinely fed from the vehicle harness through J1 (12V_KEY: J1.45↔J2.90; 12V_MR_FUSE carries F1 output), so the undriven-pin errors reflect missing PWR_FLAG markers rather than missing supplies; the pin_to_pin error reflects the J2 module symbol modelling its paralleled 5V output pins both as Power output; A1 ~FLT is an open fault output (netlist: unconnected-(A1-~FLT-Pad2)) lacking an NC flag. None indicates a physical copper fault, but unresolved errors mask any future real ERC regressions.","severity":"info","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"severity=error entries: power_pin_not_driven ×3, pin_not_connected (A1 ~FLT), pin_to_pin (J2 40/41)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets /12V_KEY (J1.45,J2.90), /5V_SENSOR_1 (J2.40,J2.41), unconnected-(A1-~FLT-Pad2)"}],"reasoning":"Evidence-supported native errors in the saved schematic; root-cause analysis shows schematic-modelling hygiene (missing PWR_FLAG/NC markers, symbol pin typing) rather than electrical faults, hence info severity. Left at defect because the native rule set is violated as saved and the errors should be resolved or waived explicitly."}]}}}
